      "writtenOn": "2023-06-05T20:41:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you sure that those bits should be removed ?\n\nActive bits may indicate inactive packets\n\n7.1.14 Change Connection Packet Type command\n```\nFor ACL Link_Type\nFor SCO Link Type\nReturn parameters:\nNone.\nEvent(s) generated (unless masked away):\nWhen the BR/EDR Controller receives the\nHCI_Change_Connection_Packet_Type command, BR/EDR the Controller\nshall send the HCI_Command_Status event to the Host. In addition, when the\nLink Manager determines the packet type has been changed for the\nconnection, the Controller on the local device will send an\nHCI_Connection_Packet_Type_Changed event to the Host. This will be done\nat the local side only.\nBit Number Parameter Description\n1 2-DH1 shall not be used.\n2 3-DH1 shall not be used.\n3 Ignored; DM1 may be used whether or not this bit is set.\n4 DH1 may be used.\n8 2-DH3 shall not be used.\n9 3-DH3 shall not be used.\n10 DM3 may be used.\n11 DH3 may be used.\n12 2-DH5 shall not be used.\n13 3-DH5 shall not be used.\n14 DM5 may be used.\n15 DH5 may be used.\nAll other bits Reserved for future use.\n```",
      "revId": "ca83ca06093581090e13f5b33c9f7d5efbb46200",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e485408e_8fcd2fc7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1495515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-05T23:06:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding of the intent of the supported/unsupported bits, as set by PeerPacketTypes, is that packet type bits set in \u0027unsupported\u0027 should negate bits set in \u0027supported\u0027. \n\nIn the snoop log attached to the bug, frame 264, the peer device doesn\u0027t indicate support for any optional packet types. In particular, EDR ACL 2Mbps and 3Mbps mode bits are both false. This results in \u0027unsupported\u0027 bits being set for all 2Mbps and 3Mbpbs modes. \n\nThe current code \u0027adds\u0027 (boolean OR) those \u0027unsupported\u0027 bits to the set of supported packet types, which then show up as requested from the host in the Change Connection Packet Type command (frame 272 in the snoop log).\n\nInstead, it seems to me, any set \u0027unsupported\u0027 bits should be \u0027subtracted\u0027 (boolean AND NOT) from those set by the \u0027supported\u0027 bits. This would be required for a peer device that declares support for 3 slot packets, but not 2Mbps, for example.\n      Thanks,\n            Blair",
      "parentUuid": "5b53421c_6fe3b8d2",
      "revId": "ca83ca06093581090e13f5b33c9f7d5efbb46200",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
